# Local Docker sidecars (LuminaryWorks ecosystem)

Idle products must not burn Docker Desktop CPU/RAM. Demo generators and heavy optional services are **opt-in** and must not restart forever on failure.

## Required

- Default `docker compose up` starts only the product **core** (API/DB/web or documented minimal set).
- Lavfi/ffmpeg publishers, synthetic cameras, Ollama, SFU, Doris, SeaTunnel, etc. use Compose **profiles** (or a clearly named overlay).
- Lab/demo generators use `restart: on-failure:N` (small N) or `restart: "no"` — not infinite `unless-stopped`.
- One publisher per MediaMTX / ZLM / SFU path. Distinct paths if multiple lab publishers exist.
- Install/public overlays must **not** remap conflicting publishers onto the same catch-all profile (e.g. do not put VistaCast `rtsp-publisher` + `rtmp-publisher` both under `ai`).
- Document stop vs destroy when using `unless-stopped` (Desktop reboot revives stopped-but-not-removed containers).

## Forbidden

- Default-on demo stream / load generators with no real traffic value
- Two services publishing the same stream path
- `restart: unless-stopped` on disposable lab publishers that exit non-zero on publish failure
- Collapsing `rtsp` + `ingest` (or similar) demo publishers into one profile without distinct paths

